.TH BPFC.CONF 5 "October 2026" "bpfc" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
bpfc.conf \- bpfcd configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/bpfc/bpfc.conf
holds
.IB key " = " value
lines;
.B #
starts a comment. Unknown keys or invalid values are errors: bpfcd refuses to
start, and on reload keeps its previous settings. Changes apply on reload,
except
.BR state_dir ,
which needs a restart.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.BI config_dir " = " /etc/bpfc/interfaces.d
Directory holding
.IB interface / direction / priority .bpfc
program files.
.TP
.BR on_external_change " = " reinstall | log
What to do when a program bpfcd installed is removed or replaced by anything
else.
.B reinstall
(default) puts bpfcd's program back and logs a warning.
.B log
logs a warning and marks the program
.B removed-externally
or
.B replaced-externally
in
.BR bpfcctl (8)
until the next reload.
.TP
.BI reinstall_limit " = " 5
Automatic reinstalls allowed per program per minute. When exceeded, bpfcd
logs an error and leaves the program alone (status
.BR reinstall-limit )
until the next reload, so it never fights another tool indefinitely. 0 means
unlimited.
.TP
.BR remove_on_stop " = " no | yes
Detach all managed programs when bpfcd stops. By default programs stay
attached across restarts and upgrades.
.TP
.BI map_dir " = "
Directory for pinned eBPF maps, passed to bpfc as
.BR \-m .
Empty means bpfc's default,
.IR /sys/fs/bpf .
.TP
.BI compile_timeout " = " 30
Seconds one bpfc run may take before it is killed and treated as a failure.
.TP
.BR log_level " = " error | warning | info | debug
Default
.BR info .
.TP
.BI bpfc_path " = " /usr/sbin/bpfc
The bpfc binary. Must be absolute.
.TP
.BI state_dir " = " /run/bpfc
Where the state file, PID file and failure logs live.
.SH NETWORK NAMESPACES
A bpfcd started with
.BI \-n " name"
reads
.I /etc/bpfc/netns/<name>/bpfc.conf
instead. When that file does not exist, the settings above except the paths
come from
.IR /etc/bpfc/bpfc.conf .
Paths default to
.I /etc/bpfc/netns/<name>/interfaces.d
(config_dir),
.I /run/bpfc/netns/<name>
(state_dir) and
.I /sys/fs/bpf/netns/<name>
(map_dir). Two more settings say where the namespace is; they are only valid in
a namespace's own file, and only one of them may be set:
.TP
.BI netns_path " = " /path
A network namespace file, or a symbolic link (or chain of links) to one, such
as
.IR /run/netns/<x> ,
.I /proc/<pid>/ns/net
or a link a container runtime hook maintains. Absolute. Followed again every
second, so pointing the link elsewhere moves bpfcd's programs to the new
namespace. Default:
.IR /run/netns/<name> .
.TP
.BI netns_veth " = " interface
The host-side end of a veth pair whose other end is in the namespace, for
example a pod's or container's veth. bpfcd follows the peer: a new veth of that
name in another namespace moves the programs there.
.PP
See
.BR bpfcd (8),
.BR "Network namespaces" .
.SH REST API
.TP
.BI rest_socket " = " /run/bpfc/bpfcd.sock
Serve the REST API (see
.BR bpfcd (8),
.BR "REST API" )
on this unix socket. Absolute, at most 107 bytes. Empty (the default): off.
A stale socket at the path is replaced; any other file there is left alone and
the API stays off. For a namespace, use its own file, for example
.IR /run/bpfc/netns/<name>/bpfcd.sock .
.TP
.BI rest_socket_owner " = " root:bpfc
Owner of the socket:
.IB user : group\fR,
.I user
or
.BI : group\fR;
names from
.I /etc/passwd
and
.IR /etc/group ,
or numbers (for accounts from a directory service). A missing part is root.
.TP
.BI rest_socket_mode " = " 0660
Permission bits of the socket, in octal. Everyone who can connect can read
and change programs.
.TP
.BI rest_dir " = " /var/lib/bpfc/interfaces.d
Where programs written through the API are kept. Files here override the
file at the same place in
.BR config_dir ,
which must be a different directory. Default in a namespace:
.IR /var/lib/bpfc/netns/<name>/interfaces.d .
.PP
These are paths, so a namespace without its own bpfc.conf does not take them
from the global file: its REST API is off unless set there (or through
.BR BPFCD_REST_SOCKET ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Each setting can be overridden by an environment variable named
.B BPFCD_
followed by the setting in capitals, for example
.B BPFCD_REMOVE_ON_STOP=yes
or
.BR BPFCD_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/bpfc .
Variables take precedence over the file and are validated the same way.
This is mainly for containers; see
.BR bpfcd (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bpfcd (8),
.BR bpfcctl (8),
.BR bpfc (8)
